From b37911fdcb5c2548e7d6808a3dadb9dc3c01ba78 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vita-build <vita@build>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 14:09:01 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Vita: menus without vitaGL's whole-texture copies, readbacks
 from the right rows, a capped decode burst, the [present] line

The menus' slow frames: a blit, a texture store write or a movie picture right after a draw made
vitaGL copy the whole texture first (glTexSubImage2D on a texture drawn in the last 4 frames: 1-2
MB read from GPU memory). Those textures are now written in place: the texture store keeps up to
8 copies, each with a write generation per 16x16 cell, and a write after a draw goes to a copy no
draw of the last 4 frames used, which takes only the cells it lacks; blits and movie pictures take
a free texture of a pool (6 and 5). With none free it is vitaGL's copy again; THPS_GL_INPLACE=0
goes back to vitaGL's copies everywhere (an A/B switch).

The menus' black boxes and stale strips: vitaGL's glReadPixels on a framebuffer object reads rows
from height - y - h (the wrong end for any partial read) and waits for the GPU only when that
framebuffer is being drawn. ReadPixels and ReadArea now glFinish and read the base target's
texels directly (row y is VRAM row y). The frontend reads the screen once (EraseSprite,
SlicedImage, the options screens' saved background) and blits it back every frame.

The copy shader finds its texel from an interpolated VRAM position, not gl_FragCoord. At most 8
new texture-cache pages are decoded a frame (a level's first frame wanted 89: 0.77 s); the rest
keep the emulated lookup a frame or two. With the profile, a [present] line every second splits a
present (flush, prepare, movie picture, swap, the rest) and times texture store writes, blits and
readbacks anywhere; [stall] adds upload and blit; [gl] counts cells written in place, new copies,
vitaGL copies, pooled blits and deferred decodes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
